A||||5||Loki||Anyone have an EGR valve explode?||||1||
Z||000000||Loki||05-16-2001||11:52 AM||||Was driving home last weekend and car started acting funny..I made it home and check everything out... The EGR had basically exploded. The top part had come apart deom base but held together by the little valve rod..Was a sight see.. And was glad it was nothing to bad.. Will get a pic up once I can find my friends Digital Camera.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||DavidHenshaw||05-16-2001||09:30 PM||||My EGR valve hasn't exploded but I think it has quit working. My idle went up suddenly so I did the vaccum test outlined in the Haynes manual and couldn't draw a vaccum on the valve. The bolts holding it down are so rusted it may take a week of WD 40 to get them off. <P>I feel like the cow who stood at the front of the classroom and read his poem. "Damn the electric fence; damn the electric fence."<P>Dave<P>86 GT<P><BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||CanadianGT||05-16-2001||11:01 PM||||Same thing happend to mine Loki.  I was driving back to school from my lunch break with a Friend and my car was sputtering, and then all of a suden dies.  I had to park the car where it was and run to school so I was not late for class.  After school I got it and took it to the school autoshop, and when I opend my decklid to show my shop teacher, we saw that the actual EGR had Popped right off the base and was dangling from a little steel rod!  Quite a sight!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Loki||05-16-2001||11:36 PM||||Wxactly what happend to me..At highway speeds it runs fine..But at start up or red lights, it wants to die...Was a sight to see..Glad it wasnt anyhting bad<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||2xsess||05-17-2001||02:43 PM||||I had one do that on my 88GT.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||05-17-2001||02:59 PM||||Let this be a lesson to all of you<P>Never never NEVER play any version of 'pop goes the weazel' on the audio system of your Fiero.<P>||||reg||1
